  :notes
    "PLAN inference apply gate v1 layered on top of the wave-18 / task 06 deterministic engine and the wave-20 / task 07 LLM-augmented `sonnet_suggest` mode. The wave-21 review surfaced wave-18 ApplySafe as too lenient (it auto-applied high-confidence slots silently); the new opt-in `apply_inferred_fields=true` flag turns inference into an EXPLICIT operator approval surface while keeping the wave-18 default byte-shape intact for back-compat callers. Apply gate (compute_apply_gate, pure function): when requested, promotes ONLY (a) deterministic high-confidence + no-conflict + caller-slot-empty fields, AND (b) wave-20 LLM proposals where the caller explicitly named the field in `llm_caller_approved` (object {field: bool} OR array of field strings) AND confidence ∈ {high, medium} AND conflict_status=none AND a per-field safety check passes. Safety check mirrors the wave-21 / task 04 conservative whitelists: target ∈ {mission_execution, mission_task_delegate, mission_flow_run}; dispatch_strategy ∈ {resident-lisp, fresh-code-alignment, agent-team, mixed} (prompt-fallback / unknown deliberately excluded — the apply gate refuses to promote them even if the LLM proposed them with high confidence + caller approval); acceptance_mode validated via canonicalize_acceptance_mode; owned_files non-empty array of non-blank strings; target_project non-empty string; workstation_dispatch boolean. Caller-vs-inferred conflicts NEVER apply (they surface on conflict_fields[] AND a mirroring skip row with reason `caller_value_conflict` so a single grep over skipped_fields[] tells observers WHY the field did not promote). Sub-threshold suggestions never apply (reason `below_apply_threshold`). Persistence boundary v1 (CRITICAL invariant): the v1 gate NEVER mutates persisted plan.sexp_text — `apply_gate.persist_inference_applied` is hard-pinned to false in to_response_json. The `persist_inference=true` flag is echoed on the block as `persist_inference_requested` so a future wave (when the persisted plan write lands) can pivot on the same wire string without breaking back-compat callers. Per the goal contract: persisted plan text is mutated only when an existing action already has `persist=true` (compile path) or this explicit `persist_inference=true` flag is supplied (execute path); the v1 gate audit-records the request without acting on it. Strict shape validation runs pre-flight (BEFORE the plan DB read) so a typo (`apply_inferred_fields=\"true\"` literal string) fails fast with INVALID_PARAM rather than silently being treated as false; only bool form accepted for apply_inferred_fields/persist_inference; only object/array for llm_caller_approved (bool/string/number rejected). attach_apply_gate_block mirrors attach_inference_block / attach_workstation_proposals_block: structured errors propagate untouched, pre-existing keys preserved (NEVER overwritten), splices the gate block onto every successful dispatch branch (executing / dispatch_skipped / dry_run / inner_error / safe-descriptor / bridge / preview short-circuit / sonnet_suggest short-circuit). The execute action surfaces the gate block uniformly across all branches. Wave-18 ApplySafe back-compat: when `apply_inferred_fields` is absent, the existing apply_safe_augmentation runs unchanged (preserves wave-18..20 byte-shape exactly). When `apply_inferred_fields=true`, the augmentation is driven from the structured `applied_fields[]` (which excludes conflicts AND respects LLM caller approval) — the dispatch then runs against the conservatively-augmented args. Either way, the gate block lands on the response so observers can audit the decision. plan_dag.rs is in :write-scope but unchanged in v1: the DAG path already rejects sonnet_suggest at preflight (wave-20 / task 07 enforcement) and the dag_v1 inference branch reuses the same wave-18 ApplySafe back-compat surface; per-node DAG apply gate composition is left to a future wave. MCP plan.rs gains three new properties (apply_inferred_fields / llm_caller_approved / persist_inference) plus a long English description pinning every invariant + a bilingual paragraph in the Chinese tool description footer cross-referencing the forward Lisp authority (intent-tools.lisp :: implemented-surface mission_plan :: :execute-contract :apply-inferred-fields-gate). Acceptance: plan_dag::tests 249/249 (unchanged); plan::tests 271/271 (+22 new); cargo test -p missiond-daemon 1392/1392 (+22 net); cargo test -p missiond-mcp --lib 17/17; cargo build --workspace clean; check-architecture-lisp --all-v2 20 files; git diff --check no whitespace. Pre-commit task-scope-guard --mode staged: 2 staged files all in :write-scope (no out-of-scope leakage; .missiond/tasks/wave21/shared-memory.lisp + report file deliberately NOT staged per wave21 protocol). Post-commit verify-task-contract.mjs: a18200b007a1 against contract OK. Apply gate flags: apply_inferred_fields (bool, default false), llm_caller_approved (object {field: bool} OR array of strings, default empty set), persist_inference (bool, default false). Safety rules: deterministic apply requires high confidence + no conflict + caller-slot-empty; LLM apply requires explicit caller approval + safety whitelist + confidence != low + conflict_status=none + caller-slot-empty + slot-not-already-promoted. Persistence boundary: v1 NEVER mutates plan.sexp_text; persist_inference flag echoed for audit only. Relationship to wave-20 / task 07 sonnet_suggest: wave-20 was propose-only (applied=false hard-pinned); wave-21 / task 05 introduces the conditional apply path under strict gates (opt-in flag + per-field caller approval + safety check + confidence check + conflict check + slot-availability check). Each barrier is independently observable on the response (skipped_fields[].reason) so an operator can debug exactly which gate fired."
